.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt MBTOWC 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mblen ,
.Nm mbtowc ,
.Nm wctomb ,
.Nm mbstowcs ,
.Nm wcstombs ,
.Nm wcstoimax ,
.Nm wcstoumax
.Nd C-locale multibyte and wide character conversion
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In stdlib.h
.Ft int
.Fn mblen "const char *s" "size_t n"
.Ft int
.Fn mbtowc "wchar_t *pwc" "const char *s" "size_t n"
.Ft int
.Fn wctomb "char *s" "wchar_t wc"
.Ft size_t
.Fn mbstowcs "wchar_t *pwcs" "const char *s" "size_t n"
.Ft size_t
.Fn wcstombs "char *s" "const wchar_t *pwcs" "size_t n"
.In inttypes.h
.Ft intmax_t
.Fn wcstoimax "const wchar_t *nptr" "wchar_t **endptr" "int base"
.Ft uintmax_t
.Fn wcstoumax "const wchar_t *nptr" "wchar_t **endptr" "int base"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The library implements the C locale alone.
Its multibyte encoding has no shift state and one byte per character,
so
.Dv MB_CUR_MAX
and
.Dv MB_LEN_MAX
are 1.
A byte converts to the wide value of the same number read as
.Vt unsigned char ,
and only the wide values 0 to
.Dv UCHAR_MAX
have a multibyte form.
.Pp
.Fn mblen
returns 0 for a null
.Fa s
or a null byte, -1 when
.Fa n
is 0, and 1 otherwise.
.Fn mbtowc
returns the same values and stores the wide value through
.Fa pwc
when
.Fa pwc
is not null.
.Fn wctomb
returns 0 for a null
.Fa s ,
stores one byte and returns 1 for a representable
.Fa wc ,
and returns -1 for any other value.
.Pp
.Fn mbstowcs
and
.Fn wcstombs
convert a string, storing at most
.Fa n
elements, the terminating null among them when it fits, and return the
count stored without the null.
.Fn wcstombs
returns
.Po Vt size_t Pc Ns \-1
when it reaches an unrepresentable value before the limit.
A null destination, which POSIX admits, counts the whole conversion and
stores nothing.
.Pp
.Fn wcstoimax
and
.Fn wcstoumax
are the wide forms of
.Fn strtoimax
and
.Fn strtoumax ,
with the same subject sequence and the same results.
An element above 0xff is none of the characters that sequence accepts.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr strtol 3 ,
.Xr strtoul 3
.Sh STANDARDS
These functions conform to
.St -isoC-99
as amended by ISO/IEC 9899:2018, sections 7.22.7, 7.22.8 and 7.8.2.4,
for the C locale.
